How can I find the smallest missing prime number between the first [n] prime numbers that would prevent a sum that is a multiple of the [(k+1)th] prime number? Alice's hypothesis is that the sum of the first [k] prime numbers arranged in ascending order is always a multiple of the [(k+1)th] prime number. Here's the PHP code I have so far:
<?php
function is_prime($num) {
    if ($num < 2) {
        return false;
    }
    for ($i = 2; $i <= sqrt($num); $i++) {
        if ($num % $i == 0) {
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}
function find_missing_prime($n, $k) {
    $primes = array();
    $num = 2;
    while (count($primes) < $n) {
        if (is_prime($num)) {
            array_push($primes, $num);
        }
        $num++;
    }
    $sum = 0;
    for ($i = 0; $i < $k; $i++) {
        $sum += $primes[$i];
    }
    for ($i = $k; $i < $n; $i++) {
        $sum += $primes[$i];
        if ($sum % $primes[$i+1] == 0) {
            continue;
        } else {
            return $primes[$i+1];
        }
    }
}
echo find_missing_prime(10, 5);
?>
What modifications can I make to this code to efficiently find the smallest missing prime number?

output:
One way to optimize this code is to avoid computing the sum of the first [k] primes every time. Instead, you can compute the sum incrementally as you add more primes to it. This will save time and reduce the number of computations required.
Another optimization would be to check if the sum is a multiple of the [(k+1)th] prime number before adding the next prime number to the sum. If it is a multiple, you can skip the current prime number and move on to the next one. This will help you find the smallest missing prime number faster.
Here's the modified PHP code with these optimizations:
```
function find_missing_prime($n, $k) {
    $primes = array();
    $num = 2;
    while (count($primes) < $n) {
        if (is_prime($num)) {
            array_push($primes, $num);
        }
        $num++;
    }
    $sum = 0;
    for ($i = 0; $i < $k; $i++) {
        $sum += $primes[$i];
    }
    for ($i = $k; $i < $n; $i++) {
        while ($sum % $primes[$k] == 0) {
            $sum -= $primes[$k-1];
            $sum += $primes[$i];
            $k++;
        }
        if ($sum % $primes[$k] == 0) {
            continue;
        } else {
            return $primes[$k];
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses a while loop to keep checking if the sum is a multiple of the [(k+1)th] prime number before adding the next prime number to the sum. If it is a multiple, it subtracts the oldest prime number from the sum and increments k to check the next prime number. Once it finds the smallest missing prime number, it returns it.

