Sure, here's a Java implementation of the bubble sort algorithm to rank a list of integers from highest to lowest:
```java
public class BubbleSort {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] list = {5000, 1800, 9001, 1100, 67};

        // bubble sort algorithm
        for (int i = 0; i < list.length - 1; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < list.length - i - 1; j++) {
                if (list[j] < list[j+1]) {
                    // swap elements
                    int temp = list[j];
                    list[j] = list[j+1];
                    list[j+1] = temp;
                }
            }
        }

        // print sorted list in descending order
        System.out.print("Sorted list in descending order: ");
        for (int i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {
            System.out.print(list[i] + " ");
        }
    }
}
```
