How can we use PHP to manipulate and display data from a MySQL database in a more efficient way?
One example is through the use of pagination. By limiting the number of records displayed on a single page, we can improve the loading speed and user experience. Here is an example code:
<?php 
  // Connect to the database 
  $conn = mysqli_connect("localhost", "username", "password", "database"); 
  // Set the number of records to display per page 
  $records_per_page = 10; 
  // Determine the page number from the URL parameter 
  $page = isset($_GET['page']) ? $_GET['page'] : 1; 
  // Calculate the starting record for this page 
  $start_from = ($page - 1) * $records_per_page; 
  // Retrieve the data from the database 
  $query = "SELECT * FROM table LIMIT $start_from, $records_per_page"; 
  $result = mysqli_query($conn, $query); 
  // Display the data in a table 
  echo "<table>"; 
  while($row = mysqli_fetch_assoc($result)) { 
    echo "<tr>"; 
    echo "<td>" . $row['id'] . "</td>"; 
    echo "<td>" . $row['name'] . "</td>"; 
    echo "<td>" . $row['other_column'] . "</td>"; 
    echo "</tr>"; 
  } 
  echo "</table>"; 
  // Calculate the number of pages 
  $query = "SELECT COUNT(*) as total FROM table"; 
  $result = mysqli_query($conn, $query); 
  $row = mysqli_fetch_assoc($result); 
  $total_pages = ceil($row['total'] / $records_per_page); 
  // Display the pagination links 
  echo "<div>"; 
  for ($i=1; $i<=$total_pages; $i++) { 
    echo "<a href='?page=$i'>" . $i . "</a> "; 
  } 
  echo "</div>"; 
?>
In this code, we use PHP to retrieve data from a MySQL database and display it in a table. We also implement pagination to limit the number of records displayed on each page, improving performance and user experience.

